scale the noise is unitary folding [15, 35]. A more targeted
way in which the noise can be scaled is to apply layerwise
folding, as proposed in, for instance, [36, 37]. Instead of
increasing the depth of the entire circuit considered as
a single global entity, layerwise folding acts on specific
layers of the circuit (see Figure 1).
